Description: Give every VP2 picture a motion-vector slot no reference holds
 PBSP stores each picture's motion vectors in a slot of mbring, where a
 later B picture reads them for direct prediction from its co-located
 picture. A surface got its slot once and kept it, but a slot is free for
 another surface whenever this one leaves the reference list, so a
 recycled surface could overwrite the vectors of a reference still in use;
 non-reference pictures always wrote slot 0. B pictures then predicted
 from the wrong vectors and differed from a software decoder in moving
 areas. Each picture now takes its surface's slot only when no reference
 in use holds it, and a free one otherwise; the second field of a frame
 keeps the slot of the first.
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv84_video_bsp.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv84_video_bsp.c
index f988d0a..e910369 100644
